NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1026,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,2,4,3,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.0868,"rank":0.1503,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV002502","role":"target","render":{"description":"A pool in which a mill sank; a pool in which hay wagons vanished and in which a coach disappears after a voice in the water asked where the man is, for the time has come. A will-o'-the-wisp above the pool means that someone will drown or that a house will be built.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45349"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV002004","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A light above a pool is seen as an omen of an accident. Later a boy drowns there who had got drunk out of grief at being rejected by a girl.","place":"Mussel","prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43322","original":"Achter de boerderij van mijn broer in Mussel was in het \"oal daip\" - de Mussel A - een diepe kolk. Zw. Tuin ziet op een avond boven die kolk een licht branden. Ze vermoedt een komend ongeluk. En dit komt.\n'n Poos later is er een feest. Een jonge man - G.D. - vraagt een meisje, of ze 's avonds met hem uit wil. Ze heeft er geen zin in. \nVan verdriet drinkt hij zich dronken.\nLater heeft 't kind spijt van haar weigering, want D. wordt de andere dag dood uit de kolk gehaald.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.955,7.03889]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV006902","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Prediction that something will happen by a canal; people with a light were seen crossing a road. Later a drowned boy was carried home along that path in the evening.","place":"Vriescheloo","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43572","original":"Veurloop.\nOabram zag nog meer. Wazzen es n poar jongelu, dei zoln troun-n. \nToun de haile boudel veurmekoar was, woln ze de meubels koopn in Winschootn. t Wicht gung dr op of en de jong zol den in Winschootn bie heur koom-m. Hai bedochde zuk en verdronk zuk in n wieke.  \nMoar, en hier gait mie t om, oal Oabram har al joarn van te veurn zegd:“Doar gunders bie de wieke gebeurt nog es n keer wat. Ik zai dr mensn deur t veld trekn; langs dei loane goan ze en koom-m bie dei boerderij oet. Misschain verdrinkt dr wel aine. Ik zai ook, dat ze n lichie bie zuk hebben.” \nEn net zo is t gebeurd. Bie oavend hebben ze de jong langs t zulfde pad van de wieke noar hoes brocht.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.06833,7.11389]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV007506","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that someone will drown in a canal within a day comes true.","place":"Veelerveen","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44134","original":"Toun ze mit t knoal aan t groaven wazzen, moz dr in t leste nog n dam deurstookn wordn.\nWazzen verschaiden manlu bie aan t waark.\nToun kwam dr aine langs, bleef n rukje stoan en zee: \n\"Joa, 't is n mooi knoal worn; t is allaind zo jammer, dat dr binnen vaarntwintig uur ain in verdrinkn mout.\"\n\"Och, doe hest altied wat\", zeden de keerls, en zai smeetn hom mit n schop vol zaand noar de kop.\nMoar kiek, d ander dag, t luip teegn twaalf uur en de mensn woln gau eetn, zee dr n seldoat teegn zien mouder:\n\"Ik goa eerst nog eevn zwemmen heur, veur t eetn.\"\n\"Och, jong, blief hier toch\", zee ze, t is muide nait meer weerd.\"\nHai gung toch hen, mor is best verdronkn.\n\nAal dizze vertelsels binnen woar.\nIk heb ze zulf beleefd.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.05583,7.12778]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Mussel.","Find Barlage on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[53.0125,7.05556],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Barlage"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.167,"rank":0.3333,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KEUNING011905","role":"member","render":{"description":"Some people hear in advance a coffin entering a house; then a death follows.","place":"Hantum","prov":"Fr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131614","original":"Der wienen guon, dy hearden, dat der earne in kiste - deakiste - yn 'e hûs brocht waerd. Dan stoar der letter ien.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEUNING013008","role":"member","render":{"description":"Many rooks are an omen of a death.","place":"Blije","prov":"Fr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131682","original":"As der in protte roeken yn 'e loft wienen, soe der ien stjerre.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KUSTERS000110","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Every evening a woman appears in the wood, until she stays away.","place":"Asten","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"C.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/207808","original":"Lang geleden kwam iedere avond n meidje over d'n Ommelsen Bos. Niemand kende haar. Ze noemden haar 't Vaal Hanneke \nOpeens bleef ze weg.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KEUNING013004","role":"member","render":{"description":"A woman knows three days in advance that someone will die.","place":"Blije","prov":"Fr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131678","original":"Oan 'e dyk wenne in âld minske, dat wist trije dagen foarút al as der ien stjerre soe.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Asten belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.0963,"rank":0.0502,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ100119","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Some children are born with a caul. They later saw everything. They could foresee death, like my uncle, who had already seen the deaths of all seven of his children in the form of little coffins on the floor.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"TM 2901","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36754","original":"Der binne bern dy wurde mei de helm geboaren. As se dy helm nei boven ta fan 't gesicht lûke, sjogge se letter alles.\nIk haw in skoansuster to Westergeast to wenjen. Dêr njonken wennet in frou dy is mei de helm geboaren.\nIn omke fan my sjocht de dea ek foarút. 't Is in Wybenga.\nSawn kear hat er in bern forlern en alle sawn kearen hat er fan tofoaren de kiste oer de flier stean sjoen. 't Is in broer fan mem. Hy wennet yn 'e Westerein.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ111712","role":"omen","render":{"description":"The seventh of seven sons is born with a caul.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29923","original":"Bontsje Keke wie mei de helm geboaren. De sawnde soan fan sawn soannen wie mei de helm geboaren.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ036709","role":"omen","render":{"description":"One of seven boys always has to get up at night to see things. He is clairvoyant.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22922","original":"Jasper en Jinke fan 'e Boelensloane hienen sawn jonges. Ien fan dy sawn jonges moest nachts ta 't hûs út om hwat to sjen. Dat wie Gerke Veenstra.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","7 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":7},"on_success":{"chime":7,"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P1","difficulty":0.9161,"rank":0.8022,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST276","role":"card","render":{"description":"The stiepelteken (mark in the doorpost) came about when a wit wief (white woman) threw the axe with which she was chasing a farmhand, and it landed in the doorpost of the barn door. The farmhand had challenged the witte wieven (white women) by bringing a spit to a spinning gathering and immediately running off again.","place":"Vasse","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"B.J.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13620","original":"Op veel plaatsen in Twente hoort men de volgende vertellingen.\nDe Witte Wiefkes hadden eens gasten of spinvisite. De knecht van een boer uit de buurt bracht er het spit heen; en toen als de wind weer terug naar huis te paard. Maar een der witte wiefkes zat hem met een bijl achterna. De knecht was echter eerder thuis. Zij wierp hem echter met de bijl na, die in den stipel (deurstijl achterdeur) bleef zitten en toen riep ze nog: \"Had ik mien eenen schoen zo gauw knupt als m'andren rupt, dan was doe 't gebraad west.\"","lang":"Standard Dutch; Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST280","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand walks past the Witte Wieven (white women) at night. Because he insults them, one of them chases him. The farmhand just manages to flee into a house. The axe the Witte Wief (white woman) threw lands in the stiepel (doorpost).","place":"Goor","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"J.W.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13624","original":"Witte Wieven waren hier bekend. Men geloofde dat ze ongeluk aanbrachten.\nEen verhaal gaat hier, dat een boerenzoon laat naat huis terugkeerde en langs een plek kwam, waar een wit wief een gebraad aan het spit ronddraaide. De boerenzoon beledigde haar, waarna het witte wief hem met een bijl achterna zette. Gelukkig voor de boerenzoon kon hij nog net de boerderij bereiken, voor het witte wief hem had ingehaald. Maar deze gooide hem nog de bijl achterna, die in de \"stiepel\" bleef zitten.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST075","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a wedding one of the guests remarks that they forgot to invite the witte wieven (white women). When someone mockingly calls out to the witte wieven, an axe is thrown at his head. He just manages to flee inside in time. The door still shows the marks of the axe. The witte wief (white woman) calls out that she could have caught him if she had not lost her little shoe.","place":"Zenderen","prov":"Ov.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"M.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13289","original":"Parallel met het verhaal van de \"spinvisite\" loopt ook 't verhaal van de \"brulfte\" (bruiloft) waar een van de gasten tegen de \"brulfteneugers\" opmerkt dat hij de \"nögste noabers\" n.l. de \"witte wieve\" heeft vergeten. De \"brulfteneuger\" laat dat niet op zich zitten, gaat naar buiten en nodigt \"de witte wieve\" uit, op spottende toon. Hij wordt onmiddelijk achterna gezeten, vlucht nog net binnenshuis, terwijl hem de bijl nagegooid wordt en 'n snee in de niendeure maakt die nog aan de kleinkinderen van het bruidspaar vertoond wordt. Hier hoort ook weer dezelfde klacht over 't schoentje bij, dat niet was vastgestrikt.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELB_13_014","role":"card","render":{"description":"A man who brings the spit to the hill of the Huns is then chased by a Hun with an axe. The man manages to get into the farmhouse; the Hun throws the axe after him, and it lands in the doorpost.","place":"Rossum","prov":"Ov.","year":1977,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128541","original":"Spit brengen\nG.M.: Ja dee knecht van Scholtn möt dat doan hebn, den hef t spit doar op n Huunboarg bracht en den hef t peard bie zik had en tenminste zoa heb ik t wa es heurd verteln en doe hef he t spit hef he doar henbracht noa n Huunboarg en doe is het der tuskn oet goan, n Huun löaw’k noa met t haandbiel en doe is Schoolt zien knecht bie t Schoolt owwer n onderstn nienduur vlögn en doe hef n Huun hem nog noasmetn en t haandbielkn in in duurnpost smetn\nE.M.: Dat heb ik ok vaak heurd.\nG.M.: Zoa heb ik t vaak heurn verteln.\nE.M.: A’j dat oppervlakkig bekiekt, zo’j zegn. Dat kan hoast geelsnich, mer ja ik heb wa honderd moal heurn verteln.","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is an object.","Begins with A. 3 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"35dbac76baf57475","accepted_hashes":["9fb1a42024e606b1d4ec21feb3dec4e77a73c70fa476f29ba3e19b370b9dcdd6","b39499dd9b578256dd12310ebab432594ada6fcf13e86d59c4c8d567f5ce5647","e694a7a0b592d1f60a1f52d8840b0e0310356259a3559e84a1a40c78bcaaf1a8"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1405,"rank":0.5773,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"BROUWERS001303","role":"member","render":{"description":"Sighting of a headless woman dressed in white.","place":"Oud-Valkenburg","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"E.H.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131805","original":"Van stropers, -----\nEen zekere S. is hier geweest --- een zekere Joep S. die deed niks anders dan stropen.\nDie heb ik eens horen vertellen dat hij hier achter in het veld, in \"der Maord Gieëlender\" (in 't Moord-Gerendal B [Brouwers]) een vrouw ---- een vrouw recht voor hem uit zag lopen ---- Zonder hoofd, ---- Zonder hoofd. En dat mens liep, hebt U niet gezien.\nJa, of zoiets nu waar is en of zo'n man dat nu maar fantaseert, dat weet ik niet, maar hij vertelde het voor echt.\n ------------\nplaats van handeling: Oud-Valkenburg \n\nvraag opn. : hoe was die vrouw gekleed?\nantw. vert. : zij droeg een lang wit kleed en liep op blote voeten. Maar ze \n zweefde meer als dat ze liep. Zo \n vertelde Joep.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BIJLSMA007508","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Someone with a death's head and glowing eyes walking about at night on hands and feet.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130658","original":"By de Burgemer tsjerke ware nachts in minske op hannen en fuotten om. Hy hie in deadsholle mei eagen as fjûr.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN007503","role":"member","render":{"description":"A headless woman roaming about at night.","place":"Leveroy","prov":"L.","year":1964,"code":null,"initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208804","original":"Vrouw zonder kop. In de buurt van deze boerderij zwierf 's nachts een vrouw rond:\"de vrouw zonder kop\". Iedereen had schrik daarvoor en 's avonds waagde zich niemand in deze omgeving.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"EGGEN001705","role":"member","render":{"description":"Meeting a white woman floating through the air.","place":"Berg","prov":"L.","year":1970,"code":null,"initials":"C.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/207880","original":"Onderwerp : wit wijf.\nTijd : einde 19de eeuw\nPlaats : Berg.\n\nIch weit noch, tot in daen tiēd mèr 'n paar hoezer in Berg sjtonge. En dao op Bemele aan, al gaar gein.\nOppenen aovend, heldere maon, gein mis of gèt, kaom 'n oud vruike nao hoēs, in Berg.\nMèh zie waor kaom aan 't begin van de grwoatstraot (grote straat), dao huërt zie geroēsj in de buim langs de weeg. Dao waor geine wind, en toch roēsjden 't. Zie kraog al gèt angs, en wol vlot wiejer loupe, pes aan de hoezer.\nMèh zie haet nog kaom eine sjtap gezat, dao kump 'n wit wiēf aangezwaef door de loch, zwoa grwoat wie 'ne wollek. \nZie ging rech-op van den angs.\nDoe die versjiening euver waor, leep dat auw minsjke wat 't loupe kòs, nao 't iërsjte hoēs.\nEn van dao haet me hör nao hoēs gebrach.","lang":"Limburgish","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Burgum belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0249,"rank":0.3559,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"TINNEV317","role":"sill","render":{"description":"A cyclist finds his way blocked in the evening by two ladies in white with horses and has to turn back (later he fell ill).","place":"Zevenaar","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22664","stain":"two"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"ENGELB_15_003","role":"card","render":{"description":"About the existence of witte wieven (white women) and the spit in the doorpost.","place":"Geesteren","prov":"Ov.","year":1979,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128566","original":"H.E.: Van de witn wiew he’j doar wa mangs van heurd?\nVr.Vr.: Van de witn wiew is ok niks van woar.\nH.E.: Nee, mer te geet ok um t verhaal, he. Joa he’j hier nog zonnen beuld, zonnen witn wievnbeuld. Ne, nee, nee (door elkaar heen gepraat, ze zijn het met elkaar niet eens)\nVr. [Wolberink, Jan]: Wat hadn ze bie ouns ok zegd, oh jee no valt mie t kenneke in zee Dat stun nog moal vuur joarn in de Twentse kraant. Als ik t met ene schoen had vastgebondn, gevondn als de ander gebondn.\nA.Ve.: ... t spit nog in n stiel van n nienduur nog zitn.\nF.Ve.: t Spit brengn.","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ031805","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a place where a murder was once committed, a man tries in vain to shoot a ghostly apparition, a white maiden.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0311","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22054","original":"By 't Blauhûs mat froeger in moart gebeurd wêze.\nLetter spoeke dêr altyd in wite juffer.\nGuon seagen dêr dy wite juffer al us rinnen. Sy woarden bang en roannen by Douwe Wynalda yn, dy't dêr tichteby wenne.\nDoe Douwe der út. Hy nom it jachtgewear mei. Hwant Douwe gong wol us op 'e jacht.\nHy seach de wite juffer ek en hy woe der op sjitte.\nMar 't gewear woe net. Doe woarde Douwe sa binaud dat hy is gau wer yn 'e hûs flucht.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"VODA_045_12","role":"card","render":{"description":"Near Montferland people sometimes heard the juffer (maiden) laughing and singing. Some have also seen her. But you must not come too close, for then she would pull you into the water.","place":"Doetinchem","prov":"Gld.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.E./J.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210863","original":"Hee vertellen mie dat as ’t water van de Rien rónd de Montferland streumen dan heurde hie mangs lachen en zingen van de juffer. En dao bunt luu, zaet e, die ze werkelijk gezeen hebt. Maor ie mót d’r niet te dichte bie komt, zeg e, want a-j te dichte bie kómt dan trekt ze oe in ’t water.","lang":"Liemers dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"LYST279","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand brings the spit to the Witte Wieven (white women). One of them chases him. The farmhand just manages to flee into a house. The axe the Witte Wief (white woman) threw lands in the stiepel (doorpost). The Witte Wief could not run faster because she had trouble with one of her shoes.","place":"Tilligte","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"B.R.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13623","original":"Door ouden wordt nog van de Wit Wieve verteld, die alleen kwaadaardig waren, wanneer ze getergd werden. Zo wordt verteld dat een boerenknecht eens het spit bracht naar de plaats, waar zij woonden. Hij werd door eene der witte wieve achtervolgd, doch hem niet kon inhalen, omdat ze in de haast maar een schoen had kunnen aantrekken. Toen de knecht het huis binnenvluchtte, wierp ze hem met een bijl achterna, die in de steil (deurpost) terecht kwam.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ034801","role":"card","render":{"description":"Witte juffers (white maidens) haunt a haunted spot.","place":"Oudega","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22700","original":"Us mem biwearde, to Aldegea spoeke it op in smel reedtsje by Jan Japiksma. Dêr wie in boskje mei in gracht der omhinne. Dêr spoeken wite juffers.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with Z.","Zevenaar. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c1","object":"window","text":"Zevenaar"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1","word":"two","stained":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.679,"rank":0.375,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST274","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a wolf at night disappears when the farmer finds a wolfskin under his bed and burns it.","place":"Drogteropslagen","prov":"Dr.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"K.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13538","original":"Vroeger was hier een knecht, die 's nachts in een wolf veranderde en het de mensen dan lastig maakte. Onder zijn bed vond de boer op zekere dag een wolfshuid en verbrandde die. Sedert was de knecht verdwenen.\n(Verteld door een zeventig-jarige).","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VVUNL301","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand becomes a werewolf by means of a leather belt, which he hides. It is found and burnt in the oven; at once the suspected farmhand comes rushing up on horseback, but he is held back, and when the belt has burnt he says: \"I am freed!\"","place":"Echt","prov":"L.","year":1920,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"F.S.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35840","original":"De weerwolf \n\nOp de hoeve Bosscherhof woonde eertijds een knecht die een lederen riem bezat, welke de macht had, hem, indien hij hem omgordde, te betoveren als weerwolf. Geheimzinnig en zorgvuldig werd deze band telkenmale door de knecht verstopt en wat men ook deed, hoe men ook spiedde, men vond hem nooit. En geregeld hadden de mensen uit de omtrek, die laat huiswaarts keerden, de weerwolf te dragen. En ook iedereen herkende steeds de knecht. Men gaf elkander raad om wanneer men overvallen werd, de weerwolf op een of andere manier te prikken of te krab-ben tot hij bloed voelde of zag. Dan was men gered. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN002605","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a black cat at midnight by means of a rim is released after the rim is burned.","place":"Baexem","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208342","original":"Volgens tweede verteller was er op Nelishof te Tungelroy een knecht die elke nacht tussen twaalf en een uur afwezig was. Door een raampje ging hij naar buiten. Hij klom dan op de schansenhoop en kwam er als kat af. De boer had hem bespied en gemerkt dat boven op de schansenhoop een velg lag van een karwiel. Die had de boer daar niet neergelegd en hij zocht verband tussen de spokerij (zwarte kat) en dat karwiel.\nDit zou hij vernietigen als de knecht afwezig was. Op zekere dag had hij hem met schapen naar Antwerpen gestuurd. Toen hij een dag weg was stak de boer zijn bakoven aan en wierp de velg erin.\nOp hetzelfde moment verscheen de knecht en wilde de oven in. Het gelukte slechts met drie man om hem daarvan te weerhouden. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Limburg an animal was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1920.","That card names an animal. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"35dbac76baf57475","accepted_hashes":["27d74dca1115dcda7e777e51d9d4630ab7ab2c0a55e735129f224c12ce377e2c","6cca289f34592abbb0bffdda4980f2bb2c833855b833051d32f6c23ed447195a","852ec172938ac1940de94fca0107cea5c2b54f222d5bf96f61f69b3647b09b0e","8fb8f253c67a81a4bdf2b3bbaf63cbe64939afa6703c31f379818f73209a89ae","e82836eb6bb6d4dc7794d947940ae6021ea310c0eaa7ffe65cc449fe5e81b50d"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2475,"rank":0.7798,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ015102","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"An impatient, rough farmer wants a large piece of land ploughed before evening. The farmhand refuses and tells the farmer he can take his proposal to the devil. The farmer takes this literally and enlists the devil's help. The next morning the land is ploughed. His dealings with the devil cost the farmer dearly: on his deathbed he was fetched by the devil.","place":"Hurdegaryp","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19770","original":"Der wie in boer, dat wie in forwoesteling. Hy wie altyd gleonhastich en net in arbeider dy't it by him úthâlde koe. Op in kear hied er wer in arbeider, doe moest der ploege wurde. It wie al let yn 'e joun en it wie ûnmooglik dy greate hoeke lân foar de nacht noch to ploeijen. Dat de arbeider sei tsjin 'e boer: \"Freegje de duvel, dat dy it docht.\" De boer sei: \"Dat dog ik\" en hy die it ek.\nDe oare moarns wie it stik lân ploege.\nMar hy hat it sûr bikeapje matten. Doe't er op syn stjerbêd lei, hat de duvel him helle.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"member","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":null,"initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"ENGELS000115","role":"member","render":{"description":"Werewolf leaps on people in the evening; as a helper with work; transformation into a werewolf by putting on a hidden coat, release after the coat is burned.","place":"Helden","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/57969","original":"Weerwolven:\nMannen, die wat laat op de baan waren, werden, vooral in donkere, stormachtige nachten soms besprongen door de weerwolf. Dit spookdier met gloeiende ogen sprong hen op de rug, en klemde zich met de voorpoten om hun nek. Ze bleven zich als een zware last aan de verschrikte man klemmen totdat hij ergens een huis bereikte. In de Broekbeemd, tussen Onder-Eijndt en Zandberg, stond ergens een holle eiken knot of poesjt. Er was een man, die als weerwolf bekend werd. Hij had een aparte jas; als hij deze aantrok werd hij weerwolf. Na zijn nachtelijke tochten verborg hij deze jas in die holle “poesjt”. Zijn buurlui ontdekten dit, en staken de “poesjt” met de jas in brand. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KEMP298","role":"member","render":{"description":"A tenant farmer finds out that a young shepherd on his farm is probably a werewolf. He sends him away for a day, and he and his farmhands discover a wolfskin in a hollow willow. They set fire to it at home. The shepherd then comes back at a furious pace and tries to grab his skin back. When he fails, the shepherd flees to the hollow tree and is never seen again.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43423","original":"Het weerwolfsvel verbrand\n\nBij de pachter van de boerderij bij het kasteel Geusselt onder Amby diende eens een scheper, een klein manneke, dat de naam had een weerwolf te zijn. 's Nachts was hij nooit in bed te vinden, maar 's morgens lag hij er weer in. De knechts van de hoeve hadden dat al dikwijls bemerkt.\nWijl dit zo opvallend was, werd zijn doen en laten gedurig bespied en zo bemerkte men dan ook dat hij, wanneer hij 's avonds uit zijn bed kroop, naar een weide ging, waar heel eenzaam een grote holle wilg stond. Daar verdween hij iedere keer in.\nOm het fijne van de zaak te achterhalen stuurde de pachter hem op zekere namiddag naar een dorp, dat meer dan drie uur van de hoeve lag, om daar koeien te kopen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Hurdegaryp belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.1446,"rank":0.8974,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST008","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every night at exactly twelve o'clock a farmhand takes a small hoop out of the lime tree. He hangs the hoop around his neck and turns into a werewolf. He roams about for a while and tears apart everything that comes near him. After that he becomes an ordinary person again. The farmer finds his behaviour strange and asks the priest for advice. The priest realises that the farmhand is a werewolf and advises the farmer to send the farmhand on an errand from which he can never be back home by midnight. On the agreed night the priest takes the hoop out of the tree at midnight. The farmhand is standing under that tree and sees everything. He flees and never comes back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0803","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13222","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen boerenknecht kroop 's nachts klokslag 12 uur in de lindenboom voor de boerderij. Boven in de boom hing voor gewone mensen onzichtbaar een hoepeltje. Dat hing de knecht om zijn hals. Als ie uit de boom geklauterd was, liep ie in de gedaante van een hond weg en verscheurde alles wat hem in de weg kwam. Als ie een tijd zo rondgelopen had, was ie weer gewoon mens. Na een tijd was het de boer, bij wie de weerwolf in dienst was, opgevallen, dat zijn knecht nacht op nacht weg was. Hij ging naar de pastoor en die had het zaakje meteen door. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ111718","role":"card","render":{"description":"A man out walking with a companion suspects that a man approaching them is a werewolf. When the werewolf comes closer, the man quickly throws him his red handkerchief. The werewolf then leaves the man alone. Because the two friends still want to know whether they were dealing with a real werewolf, they go to the man's house. When the man comes home, they shine a lantern in his face. The pieces of the red handkerchief are still hanging between his teeth. The man really is a werewolf.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29929","original":"Der wie in man, dy hie in gesin. Dy man wie in wjerwolf. By 't tsjuster wie er warber. Doe wie der in oaren ien dy wie mei syn maet der op út. Hja rounen togearre troch de Kûkhernster lânnen en doe kaem dy wjerwolf har tomjitte. De man, dy't mei syn maet wie fortocht de man fan dat gesin, dat dàt de wjerwolf wie, mar hy wist it net seker. Doe't dan dy wjerwolf oan harren ta wie, smiet er him gau syn reade bûsdoek ta en doe bleau de wjerwolf fan har ôf. Doe sei dy man tsjin syn maet: Litte wy ris nei dat en dat hûs ta gean - dat wie it hûs dêr't dy wjerwolf wenne. Hwant hy woe wite oft de bewenner fan dat hûs de wjerwolf wie.\nAllinne doarst hy der net hinne. Dêrom naem er syn kammeraet mei. 't Wie tusken Kûkherne en Burgumerheide. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST189","role":"door","render":{"description":"Three people tell that late one evening they met a big dog with fiery eyes that jumped on their backs. Only at the edge of the field did it jump off and vanish. The dog vanished near a farm already known as uncanny, because the farmhand there said that the cows several times jumped up at the stroke of midnight while the stable doors flew open by themselves.","place":"Puiflijk","prov":"Gld.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"C.v.d.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13453","original":"Spookdieren\nMij is eens door drie verschillende personen op zeer verschillende tijden meegedeeld dat op de Waaldijk tussen Boven-Leeuwen en Druten 's avonds in pikdonker plotseling een abnormale grote hond, die plotseling verscheen, hen zwijgend met vurige ogen volgde en even plots aan de grens van Druten verdween. Beide personen waren niet bijgelovig maar hadden van angst 't zweet op de rug staan van angst, temeer daar de hond verdween bij een boerderij waar 't niet \"pluis\" scheen te zijn. Een knecht op deze boerderij vertelde mij eens hoe verscheidene malen 's nachts de koeien om klokslag 12 uur opsprongen en staldeuren openvlogen zonder 'n aanwijsbare oorzaak. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ097803","role":"card","render":{"description":"Among seven successive brothers there is a werewolf.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36323","original":"Fan sawn jonges, dy't op elkoar folgen, wie ien in wjerwolf.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","3 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c3","object":"door","n":3},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.687,"rank":0.6437,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV013701","role":"top","render":{"description":"Ancestors keep silent about hiding a treasure, so their spirits have no rest and haunt at midnight. A farmhand addresses a spirit, which asks him whether he will carry out its task.","place":"Barger-Compascuum","prov":"Dr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44573","half":"top"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BIJLSMA008901","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"But the beachcombers chop off both her hands to take the rings, and the woman drowns. At night skippers see the woman wandering by the post, so the murder is not forgotten.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ010509","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"One evening she heard her mother's shuffling footsteps outside. The moment she saw her mother coming, she wished she were gone. The mother vanished again, and from then on the girl was at peace.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ106101","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Two weeks later the wife of that same acquaintance died.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"WEV013701","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"As a pledge the farmhand holds out a pitchfork wrapped in a handkerchief to the spirit, which takes hold of it, leaving its handprint in the handkerchief. The spirit says a treasure is hidden in a wall. After the treasure is found, all stays quiet.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"KEMP173","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Fortunately he knows that you must be bold with ghosts and never give them their way. He follows the ghost but refuses to carry out the tasks it gives him. The next day the craftsman has grey hair, but he is in possession of a treasure. From then on he can live off his wealth.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"WEV004601","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Especially people who lived wicked lives, suicides and murdered people are seen again after their death.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"VODA_002_16","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Each time a pancake is done, a limb falls out of the chimney, until at midnight they form a skeleton that comes to life. The skeleton points him to the cellar, where there are three chests of gold. When the chests are divided between the man, the church and the poor, the ghost can rest.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"CJ081006","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Then one night her mother suddenly stood before the bed. The woman was terrified and never again wished to see her mother.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"DYKFRIES2175","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Two of them boast that they could handle the minister's ghost if it appeared now. The ghost then takes the two boasters away. The third gets off with a fright. Four weeks later the two friends who were taken turn up again, but they do not tell what happened.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0477"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"CJ091406","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"But because he did not do this (he remarried), the woman could find no rest after her death and came back to haunt. Only when the widower gave his little daughter what she was entitled to did she stay away.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"VODA_013_13","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"On the priest's advice, the daughter asks on the fourth day what the spirit wants: \"I cannot obtain eternal life because I did not keep my promise to go to Kevelaer.\" Mother and daughter go on pilgrimage. They and the priest see the figure, the others do not. In Kevelaer the bells began to ring by themselves. A mass was said and the spirit disappeared.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0477"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"AMPT000301","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"When the ghost comes down the stairs, the man jumps into a room where the midwife is getting dressed.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The bottom piece mentions ‘farmhand’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c5"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c5"],"stack":["c1","c5"]},"found_card":{"card":"c5"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3006,"rank":0.8919,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ097804","role":"member","render":{"description":"On the Boppewei there is a ghost that comes a little closer every year.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36324","original":"In omke fan my fortelde ús, op 'e Boppewei ûnder 'e Westerein dêr spoeke jouns altyd in âlde hear om. Dy kom alle jierren ien hoannestap tichterby.\nSe seinen ek wol dat it in pleachbeest wie.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ111508","role":"member","render":{"description":"The ghost of a murdered girl keeps haunting.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29770","original":"Hjir op dit ein fan 't spoar is froeger ris in famke formoarde. Dat famke spûke dêr letter om, der binne forskate lju dy't har hjir wol sjoen ha. Myn suster sliepte ris in kear by de buorlju. Doe kaem dêr dy nachts dat famke foar 't glês.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2178","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"At night there was a little man outside who looked horrible. He meant no harm.","place":"Hurwenen","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/127562","original":"En dan was er nog zo'n mannegie dat er 's nachts uit moest. M'n grootvader heb 'm is opgewacht. Dat was ontzettend, zoals dat mannegie eruit zag. 't Was afschuwelijk om te zien. Maar kwaad dinne ze niemand.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ111302","role":"member","render":{"description":"At night a group of headless children wanders about by the railway bridge. They are ghost children. Nobody dares walk past the railway bridge at night.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29707","original":"By de spoarbrêge yn 'e Westerein doarmen yn 'e nacht altyd in pear berntsjes om, dy hienen gjin holtsjes.\nDêr doarsten froeger de minsken by nacht net lâns.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a werewolf.","The card about Hurwenen belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1885,"rank":0.7083,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CBAK0376","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer on a haunted farm asks a begging old soldier whether he will keep watch at night.","place":"Uitdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1903,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9190","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ081008","role":"half","render":{"description":"There at the roadside they saw a giant, fully twice the size of a normal person. A large cloak flapped around him; otherwise he stood completely still. It was a ghost.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"BIJLSMA003301","role":"half","render":{"description":"After his death his widow hears in the evenings the same sound her husband made when he went upstairs. Visitors go to look and hear knocking at a book. When it is picked up, the papers fall out of the book.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ058107","role":"half","render":{"description":"Suddenly they saw a fellow wearing a hat. When he passed them, he suddenly vanished.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CBAK0513","role":"half","render":{"description":"The answer is that they have waited a long time for someone, that there is money buried of which he may have a third, and the rest must go in equal parts to the poor and a church congregation. Once the request has been carried out, the haunting stops.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ015103","role":"half","render":{"description":"As the man and his new bride are about to get into the carriage, his dead wife suddenly appears. She reminds him of his promise and the newlyweds undo the marriage. The spirit of the dead can only find rest once a promise made before death is kept.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CBAK0376","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"At midnight, after a lot of noise, six high-ranking officers with sabres come in and go to the haystack. There they dig a hole, take out a kettle of gold coins, bury it again and leave. With a farmhand's help the beggar digs up the kettle. The next night they keep watch together and see the men come again, who leave and never come back when they find nothing. The soldier stays on the farm. According to the narrator it was providence that the soldier was meant to have the money.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401","stain":"six"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘farm’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c7","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c7"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":6,"card":"c1","word":"six","stained":"c7"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
